  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating the skewness of the lotteries—specifically, the extent to which probability is concentrated on unfavorable outcomes—and preferring the more right-skewed one. In this case, Lottery B has a slightly higher probability (99.9%) on the 0 Euro outcome compared to Lottery A (99.8%), making it marginally more right-skewed. Thus, the reason would prefer Lottery B. However, the verbal report does not mention skewness, probability distribution, or any analysis of the tail of the outcomes. Instead, it only notes that both are bad and have very little chance of winning. There is no reference to the structure of the lotteries or any reasoning about skewness. Therefore, the individual did not consider or apply the skewness-based decision reason. The information considered by the individual (low win chances, both bad) is unrelated to the skewness metric required by the reason. The justification provided (none) is absent. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
