  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness based on proportion of probability on unfavorable outcomes) is not considered by the individual. The individual focuses on the magnitude of the loss (higher loss in A) and the insignificance of the probability difference, not on the proportion of probability assigned to unfavorable outcomes. The decision reason requires comparing the proportion of probability mass on the loss side (20% vs. 25%), which would indicate B is more right-skewed. However, the individual does not mention this proportion or any analysis of distribution shape. The justification centers on loss magnitude, not skewness. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The reasoning process is inconsistent with the rule of the decision reason. The individual’s justification is based on loss severity, not on skewness or probability distribution shape.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

